Usage: agent-deck session context [id|title] [options]

Show everything that is being passed to the agent for a session: the instruction-file
hierarchy, skills, agents, tool schemas and MCP servers, ranked by what each costs.

This measures the FIXED STARTUP OVERHEAD — the bytes loaded into every turn, which is
the part you can clean up. It does not measure your conversation, which is what
usually fills a context window.

Every figure states where it came from. A number the harness measured, a number
agent-deck estimated and a number that does not exist are rendered differently, and
an unknown is never printed as zero. Harnesses with no token accounting print the
inventory with '—' for every figure and exit 0.

Options:
  -all
    	Breakdown: print every item instead of the ranked top
  -capabilities
    	Print what this harness can report, without inspecting anything
  -glossary
    	Define every word these screens use — adapter, basis, anchor, residual, CAPT/RECON/ABSENT — and exit
  -item string
    	Print one item's provenance, lever and verbatim text (id from --tab breakdown)
  -json
    	Emit the report as JSON (stable schema; carries provenance on every figure)
  -q	One-line summary (short for --quiet)
  -quiet
    	One-line summary: the gauge figure and how many items you can act on
  -strict
    	Exit 3 when the report fails its own reconciliation or breaks an invariant
  -tab string
    	Which view to print: overview, breakdown or verify (default "overview")
  -timeout duration
    	Abort inspection after this long (default 20s)
  -tolerance-pct float
    	--verify: relative tolerance, as a percentage of the harness figure (default 10)
  -tolerance-tokens int
    	--verify: absolute tolerance floor, in tokens (default 500)
  -verbose
    	Include the per-category notes explaining how each figure was obtained
  -verify
    	Compare against the harness's own accounting. MUTATES the live session: sends /context (Claude) or /status (Codex) and reads the panel back
  -verify-ready-timeout duration
    	--verify: how long to wait for the agent to go idle before typing into it (default 2m0s)
  -verify-timeout duration
    	How long to wait for the harness's own panel to render (default 30s)
  -yes
    	Skip the --verify confirmation prompt (for CI; the default always asks before typing into a session)

Examples:
  agent-deck session context my-project                  # overview
  agent-deck session context my-project --tab breakdown  # what to remove, and how
  agent-deck session context my-project --item memory:/path/to/CLAUDE.md
                                                        # one item's text (ids come from --tab breakdown)
  agent-deck session context my-project --tab verify     # the arithmetic
  agent-deck session context my-project --json | jq .    # full report
  agent-deck session context --glossary                  # what adapter, basis, anchor, CAPT, RECON… mean
  agent-deck session context my-project --capabilities   # what this harness can tell you
  agent-deck session context my-project --verify         # diff against the harness's own /context

--verify is the only part of this command that writes anything: it types the harness's own
accounting command into the live session and reads the panel back, so it asks first. It waits
for the agent to go idle and moves an unsent draft out of the composer, but the command still
joins that conversation for good. The context hotkey in the TUI never does this.

Exit codes:
  0  done; with --verify, every graded group agreed within tolerance
  1  could not run (bad arguments, no live pane, unreadable panel) — nothing was compared
  2  no session matched
  3  --strict: the report failed its own reconciliation or an invariant
  4  --verify: a group disagreed with the harness beyond tolerance
  5  --verify: nothing could be graded, so no agreement is claimed (never read this as a pass)
